@@ -10,10 +10,54 @@ Build and interface details: [documentation](https://unixnu.com/drivers/adreno-m
 
 ## Memory reuse
 
-Unused owned image backing can serve later pooled or dedicated images. Extra image spares share a 256 MiB device budget and expire after ten seconds. Plain unused backing of at least 256 KiB can be released by the existing room worker, with at most 128 MiB queued. Allocation failure reclaims queued backing before retrying. Imported memory and owner callbacks retain their release ordering.
+Unused owned image backing can serve later pooled or dedicated images. Image spares expire after ten seconds and are reclaimed on allocation failure or memory pressure; they have no byte limit. Unused buffer reservations share a separate 64 MiB device budget across memory types. The room worker rechecks demand and reuses a spare of the same pool and memory type before allocating. If foreground completions restore room during allocation, the new owned buffer stays spare with its address object intact. Plain unused backing of at least 256 KiB can be released by the existing room worker, with at most 128 MiB queued. Allocation failure reclaims queued backing before retrying. Imported memory and owner callbacks retain their release ordering.
+
+## Heap texture copies
+
+Fixed runtime-owned Private heap textures can write complete texel words directly
+to their heap buffer when the descriptor range is aligned. Tracked heaps can also
+read it directly. Untracked heaps retain their input snapshot and staging keep;
+their concurrent-writer merges use the original scratch path. Shared or imported
+memory, special surfaces and ineligible layouts retain staging. Staged output
+preserves only untouched edge ranges when that saves at least half a full copy.
+The original barriers and alias rules remain in force. CPU Vulkan checks cover
+production ShadowCopy dispatch, access stages, padding and independent writes;
+A840 frame performance requires a hardware capture.
 
 ## Frame diagnostics
 
+The iPhone24A446 build profile excludes iPad-specific image-relative QuartzCore
+reads/writes and instruction patches, retaining public environment policy only.
+An optional `NativeAdrenoMetal.fulltest` marker next to a published bundle runs
+the maintained raw/Turnip/bridge/frontend checks once in backboardd on a separate
+worker while normal discovery and presentation continue. It does not create a
+second scanout server. Individual T/M/F verdicts remain authoritative; a worker
+return is not a blanket pass. Fatal GPU/transport prerequisites still stop their
+dependent submissions. Completed text lines carry the existing wire's optional
+end marker so the kernel/USB log need not sample only the last cached row.
+
+The integrated checks reuse the published runtime's already writable cache
+directory, and drop their extra frontend-device reference after completion.
+They may create a second Vulkan instance/device while the published device is
+alive: the Darwin KMD must supply independent connection/VA/fence ownership.
+A process-global connection closed by enumeration or another device's teardown
+does not satisfy this contract. The iPhone A840 trial verified raw compute and
+triangle pixels, then exposed that lifetime conflict; complete Metal/UI
+acceptance remains separate from these shader results.
+
+The integrated worker also reuses upstream243d63c GMEM/system-memory colour
+checks on device and imported host images. The local integration declares the
+copy destination usage, performs the initial image layout transition, drains
+submitted work before teardown, and retains resources when quiescence is unknown.
+Every pixel is checked against the fixture, with setup errors kept separate.
+Bridge counters logged before cleanup are labelled `M-body cleanup-pending`;
+only the later M/F verdict records completed cleanup and frontend results.
+
+Upstream6416a76 icon-service notifications are retained in the existing event65
+channel: device and queue creation, and at most eight completed draw/dispatch
+commands. These observations do not change the iPhone process's launchd policy.
+The sheng-only Core Image environment choice is not assumed valid for iPhone27.
+
 With `sheng-gpu-trace=1` the render server writes its frame trace (command phases, encoding batches, memory decisions, completion stages, attachments and Turnip pass and submission records) to its own file. Only event 63, the render, encode and completion thread identities, reaches the kernel ring. See [GPU frame diagnostics](https://unixnu.com/porting/gpu-diagnostics) for fields and decoding.
 
 `sheng-wallpaper-freeze=1` enables wallpaper isolation. A Poster renderer freezes GPU submission after a successful command draws into and stores an IOSurface of at least two million pixels. The completed output stays retained. Later commands remain committed and unscheduled, with their resources and queue leases retained. Already submitted work completes normally. PosterBoard and other processes keep submitting. The switch defaults to off; `NATIVE_METAL_FREEZE_WALLPAPER=1` selects the same mode directly in a renderer process.
